.TH CNGPT 1 "2026-03-16" "cngpt 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cngpt \- nanoGPT in C with OpenBLAS acceleration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cngpt train
.RI [ options ]
.B \-\-data= DIR
.B \-\-weights= FILE
.br
.B cngpt sample
.RI [ options ]
.B \-\-weights= FILE
.br
.B cngpt bench
.RI [ options ]
.B \-\-weights= FILE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cngpt
is a C implementation of nanoGPT (Andrej Karpathy) using OpenBLAS for
matrix operations.
It supports full training from a pre-tokenized binary dataset, autoregressive
text generation, and a compiler-flag benchmark harness.
.PP
Model architecture matches GPT-2: transformer blocks with multi-head
causal self-attention, GELU activations, and weight-tied output projection.
Supported scales: gpt2 (117M), gpt2-medium (345M), gpt2-large (762M),
gpt2-xl (1.5B).
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS train
Train (or fine-tune) a model on pre-tokenized data.
.PP
The data directory must contain a file named
.B train.bin
with tokens stored as uint16_t in row-major order (produced by a tokenizer
script such as those from the nanoGPT repository).
.SS sample
Generate text autoregressively from a loaded checkpoint.
Sampling uses temperature scaling and optional top-k filtering.
.SS bench
Run a fixed number of inference forward passes and report throughput
(tokens/second, ms/token).
For a full compiler-flag sweep, use
.B tests/bench.sh
directly.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Common
.TP
.BI \-\-weights= FILE
Path to weight file in cngpt binary format.
For
.B train
this is the starting checkpoint (or a freshly exported HuggingFace model).
.SS train
.TP
.BI \-\-data= DIR
Directory containing
.IR train.bin .
.TP
.BI \-\-out= FILE
Checkpoint output file (default:
.IR checkpoint.bin ).
Intermediate checkpoints are written as
.IR FILE . N
every
.B \-\-save-every
steps.
.TP
.BI \-\-iters= N
Number of gradient update steps (default: 5000).
.TP
.BI \-\-batch= B
Batch size (default: 4).
Reduce if GPU (or CPU RAM) is tight.
.TP
.BI \-\-seq= T
Sequence length per example (default: 1024).
Must not exceed the model's
.I block_size
(1024 for standard GPT-2).
.TP
.BI \-\-lr= LR
Peak learning rate for cosine schedule with linear warmup (default: 3e\-4).
.TP
.BI \-\-lr\-min= LR
Minimum learning rate at the end of cosine decay (default: 1e\-5).
.TP
.BI \-\-warmup= W
Number of linear warmup steps (default: 100).
.TP
.BI \-\-dropout= D
Dropout probability applied to embeddings and residual connections
(default: 0.0 — no dropout).
.TP
.BI \-\-grad\-clip= G
Global gradient norm clip threshold (default: 1.0).
Set to 0 to disable.
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-every= N
Print average loss every
.I N
steps (default: 10).
.TP
.BI \-\-save\-every= N
Save intermediate checkpoint every
.I N
steps (default: 500).
.SS sample
.TP
.BI \-\-prompt= TEXT
Initial context string (default: begin from
.IR <|endoftext|> ).
Note: with GPT-2 BPE tokenization, proper encoding requires the Python
vocabulary; without
.B \-\-vocab
the prompt is treated as raw bytes.
.TP
.BI \-\-tokens= N
Number of new tokens to generate (default: 200).
.TP
.BI \-\-temp= F
Softmax temperature.
Values below 1.0 make output more deterministic; above 1.0 more random
(default: 1.0).
.TP
.BI \-\-topk= K
Top-k sampling: only the
.I K
highest-probability tokens are considered.
0 disables top-k and samples from the full distribution (default: 40).
.TP
.BI \-\-vocab= FILE
Path to vocabulary file (one token string per line, as exported by
.IR scripts/export_weights.py ).
Without this, token ids are printed directly.
.SS bench
.TP
.BI \-\-iters= N
Number of forward passes to time (default: 50).
.TP
.BI \-\-seq= T
Sequence length for inference benchmark (default: 128).
.SH WEIGHT FILE FORMAT
The binary weight file starts with a 7 × int32 header:
.PP
.RS
[magic=0x434E4750, version=1, n_layer, n_head, n_embd, vocab_size, block_size]
.RE
.PP
Followed immediately by float32 tensors in the order documented in
.BR model.h :
.I wte, wpe,
then for each layer:
.IR ln1_w ", " ln1_b ", " c_attn_w ", " c_attn_b ", " c_proj_w ", " c_proj_b ", "
.IR ln2_w ", " ln2_b ", " mlp_fc_w ", " mlp_fc_b ", " mlp_proj_w ", " mlp_proj_b ,
then
.IR ln_f_w ", " ln_f_b .
.PP
Use
.B scripts/export_weights.py
to generate this file from a HuggingFace GPT-2 checkpoint.
.SH DATA FORMAT
Training data is a flat binary file of uint16 token ids.
The file is memory-mapped and read sequentially; it wraps at the end.
.PP
To prepare the Shakespeare dataset from the nanoGPT repository:
.PP
.RS
.EX
python3 nanoGPT/data/shakespeare_char/prepare.py
# Produces train.bin / val.bin in that directory
.EE
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
Export GPT-2 weights:
.PP
.RS
.EX
python3 scripts/export_weights.py --model=gpt2 --out=gpt2.bin
.EE
.RE
.PP
Sample from GPT-2:
.PP
.RS
.EX
cngpt sample --weights=gpt2.bin --prompt="Once upon a time" \\
             --tokens=200 --temp=0.8 --topk=40 \\
             --vocab=gpt2.vocab.txt
.EE
.RE
.PP
Fine-tune on Shakespeare for 1000 steps:
.PP
.RS
.EX
cngpt train --data=data/shakespeare_char \\
            --weights=gpt2.bin --out=shakespeare.bin \\
            --iters=1000 --batch=2 --seq=256
.EE
.RE
.PP
Run the compiler-flag benchmark:
.PP
.RS
.EX
tests/bench.sh --weights=gpt2.bin --iters=30 --seq=128
.EE
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS
Controls the number of threads used by OpenBLAS.
The benchmark harness sweeps values 1–8.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I gpt2.bin
Default weight file location (produced by
.IR scripts/export_weights.py ).
.TP
.I gpt2.vocab.txt
Vocabulary file produced alongside the weight export.
